  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "At Imprisonment Valley he looks around and says it is here. With Frost Butterfly Warrior he faces a formation. Narration calls them two rank seven Gu Immortals from Beast Calamity grotto-heaven. He turns into a giant with bull head and human body while Frost Butterfly Warrior becomes a mini butterfly person. After their immortal killer moves break the formation, he is overjoyed that the entire valley is made of immortal materials, southern thorns.",
      "chapters": [
        1921
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_frost_butterfly_warrior",
        "sys_gu_immortal",
        "loc_beast_calamity_grotto_heaven"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Ying Wu Xie says that if he is not wrong, a transformation path Gu Immortal should be Steel Rush Warrior, Fang Yuan’s subordinate from Beast Calamity grotto-heaven, drifting in the outside world after the fate war. Fairy Zi Wei argues that even killing Steel Rush Warrior would inflict little loss on Fang Yuan.",
      "chapters": [
        2075
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "named-as-fang-yuan-subordinate",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_ying_wu_xie",
        "char_fang_yuan",
        "char_fairy_zi_wei"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Facing rock monkey Bu Tian Kong with three other warriors, he says Steel Rush and turns into a rhino person. Narration states the four cultivate transformation path, originated from Beast Calamity grotto-heaven, originally had rank seven cultivation, and with Fang Yuan’s help all became rank eight.",
      "chapters": [
        2172
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "rank-eight-rhino-form",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Bu Tian Kong’s fist smashes Steel Rush Warrior’s skull into mush, then shatters his soul. Narration states he could not be more dead, that his headless corpse falls like a broken rag doll, and that body and immortal aperture are absorbed by the great world as nutrients. All four rank eight attackers die.",
      "chapters": [
        2173
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "death-to-bu-tian-kong",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "Narration lists Steel Rush Warrior among Gu Immortals who died in Crazed Demon Cave, and states that most of them were revived through Human Sea and had to re-cultivate to become immortal again.",
      "chapters": [
        2215
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "citation_unchecked",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "human-sea-revival",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_crazed_demon_cave",
        "loc_human_sea"
      ]
    }
  ],
